{"availability":"available","full":"shaxntanu/VSCode-Portfolio","name":"VSCode-Portfolio","description":"A VS Code-themed developer portfolio showcasing projects, tech stack, and experience. Built with Next.js, TypeScript, and Framer Motion. Features interactive file explorer, animated tabs, and terminal-style UI elements.","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2025-11-25T13:23:10Z","updated":"2026-10-04T10:14:20Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://shantanu-vsc-portfolio.vercel.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://shantanu-vsc-portfolio.vercel.app/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-05T05:50:25.179Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-05T05:50:25.179Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-05T05:50:25.179Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-04T06:12:41.300Z","stars":1,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-05T05:50:25.179Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["My portfolio, designed to look like the editor I use every day","I spend most of my time in VS Code working on hardware and firmware, so I built my portfolio to match that workflow.","This is not just another themed website. It replicates VS Code's interface with a working file explorer, tab system, sidebar navigation, and a terminal-style resume viewer. The home page displays Arduino/C++ pseudo-code that describes my development process (including debugging, testing, and the occasional troubleshooting session)."],"features":["Home - Pseudo-code representation of my development workflow","About - Background, interests, and current work (includes an interactive world map)","Circuits - Embedded projects with circuit simulations, schematics, and code viewers","Coursework - Academic projects organized by year (mobile apps, image processing, simulations, AI/ML, digital logic)","Projects - Hardware modules, IoT systems, and web applications with integrated BOM viewer"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/shaxntanu/VSCode-Portfoli